      "content": "That's a decent start, it captures the vibe okay. But looking at the automated review for this draft, the \"depth score\" is way too low—like, it's flagging as a \"shallow interaction\" because the word count is so minimal. \n\nI get that I said not to pad it, but if it's too short, the system just rejects the quest file automatically. Can you expand on this? Try to dive deeper into his vision of the shattered crown or maybe describe the atmosphere of the Hollows while he's talking. Just... please keep it meaningful. I don't want a bunch of \"the fog was foggy and the mist was misty\" type stuff, I just need more actual substance so the metric doesn't kill it.",
